    "title": "Valley Weather Update: Thursday's System to Bring Rain, Maybe a Little Snow - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Joe Ebner ,\n1 days ago Dry weather continues on our Wednesday under high pressure. We will see increasing clouds and an uptick in wind speeds as a weak low crosses east over the upper Great Lakes. There isn’t much potential for rain from this due to the distance from our location and a lack of substantial moisture. Temperatures today should range in the mid to upper 40s this afternoon across our area. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
